;
; DiagnosticCodes — the TS error numbers, ported from the reference's
; internal/diagnostics/diagnostics_generated.go.
;
; GENERATED by packages/tscaly/tools/gendiagnostics.py. Do not edit; edit the
; generator. Regenerate after a submodule pin bump.
;
; ONE INTEGER PER MESSAGE, and no text. The yardstick compares a diagnostic's
; code and span; the message string lives in a table this port has no reason to
; carry, and TESTPLAN.md says so where it lists what the dump format does not
; show — a wrong message with a right code passes here.
;
; The set is exactly the messages the reference's scanner.go, parser.go,
; jsdoc.go and binder.go reference, deduped. The NAMES are the reference's own
; Go identifiers with a
; `Diag` prefix and nothing else changed, so a site in our scanner spells the
; same name as the site in theirs and the two can be diffed by grep.
;
; Sorted by CODE rather than by name, because that is the order a failing
; diff prints them in.

